1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,399
Two people land in the United Kingdom on
the very same day. One flew in from

2
00:00:05,419 --> 00:00:10,254
Lagos. The other from Dhaka. Same airport.
Same suitcase. Same two thousand

3
00:00:10,274 --> 00:00:10,707
pounds.

4
00:00:11,627 --> 00:00:16,276
Thirty days later... one of them is broke,
in debt, and sleeping on a friend's

5
00:00:16,296 --> 00:00:16,575
sofa.

6
00:00:17,445 --> 00:00:22,786
The other one has a bank account, a
doctor, a job search already running, and

7
00:00:22,806 --> 00:00:28,147
— this is the part nobody believes — most
of that money is still in the bank.

8
00:00:28,917 --> 00:00:33,416
The difference was not luck. It was not
money. It was the order they did things

9
00:00:33,436 --> 00:00:33,588
in.

10
00:00:34,758 --> 00:00:39,283
So if you have just arrived in the UK, or
you are about to... stay with me.

11
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:43,768
I will tell you what to do first, what to
do next, and, just as important,

12
00:00:43,788 --> 00:00:44,798
what to never do.

13
00:00:46,118 --> 00:00:51,387
One important thing before we start.
Everything in this video is correct as

14
00:00:51,407 --> 00:00:52,586
of November 2026.

15
00:00:53,256 --> 00:00:57,622
The UK changes its rules often, sometimes
without much warning.

16
00:00:58,292 --> 00:01:03,346
So please... before you act on anything I
say, check the official GOV.UK website,

17
00:01:03,366 --> 00:01:08,231
or the NHS website for anything about
health. I will remind you along the way,

18
00:01:08,251 --> 00:01:10,862
and I will show you exactly where to look.

19
00:01:11,732 --> 00:01:14,849
Kiran: Rule zero. Check GOV.UK. Always.

20
00:01:15,419 --> 00:01:16,365
Chidi: Even on a Sunday?

21
00:01:17,036 --> 00:01:18,678
Kiran: Especially on a Sunday.

22
00:01:19,898 --> 00:01:24,508
Mr Deal: Welcome to the UK! You need the
newest phone! And a laptop! Only twenty-

23
00:01:24,528 --> 00:01:25,271
months to pay!

24
00:01:25,791 --> 00:01:28,026
Chidi: Yes! The newest phone! And the
laptop! Take my money!

25
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:30,185
No. No, no, no. Please. Do not.

26
00:01:30,955 --> 00:01:35,150
Your first month is not about having nice
things. It is about having a safe

27
00:01:35,170 --> 00:01:38,916
place to sleep, a way to earn, and money
left over for emergencies.

28
00:01:39,686 --> 00:01:44,221
Every new phone, every new laptop, every
new sofa you buy in week one, is money

29
00:01:44,241 --> 00:01:48,546
you cannot use when something goes wrong.
And in a new country... something

30
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:50,103
always goes a little wrong.

31
00:01:50,873 --> 00:01:55,402
So here is the golden rule. Buy only what
you need this week. Everything else

32
00:01:55,422 --> 00:01:56,643
can wait thirty days.

33
00:01:57,413 --> 00:02:02,097
Need a phone? A used one works exactly the
same. Need furniture? Charity shops,

34
00:02:02,117 --> 00:02:06,621
Facebook Marketplace, Vinted, and local
free groups are full of good things.

35
00:02:06,641 --> 00:02:10,670
Nobody here will judge you for it.
Honestly, half of the UK does it.

36
00:02:11,290 --> 00:02:14,261
Kiran: Used phone. Same screen. Zero
stress.

37
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:15,917
Chidi: But it is not shiny...

38
00:02:16,838 --> 00:02:18,540
Kiran: Shiny is expensive, Chidi.

39
00:02:19,809 --> 00:02:24,338
Step one, before anything else. Make sure
you can prove who you are, and that

40
00:02:24,358 --> 00:02:26,405
you are allowed to be here, online.

41
00:02:27,075 --> 00:02:32,518
The UK is moving away from the plastic BRP
card. For most people now, your

42
00:02:32,538 --> 00:02:37,390
immigration status lives in a digital
eVisa inside a UKVI account.

43
00:02:38,161 --> 00:02:42,463
Employers, landlords, and banks will ask
you for a share code. That is a short

44
00:02:42,483 --> 00:02:46,674
code you create yourself, from your
account, in about a minute. It lasts for

45
00:02:46,694 --> 00:02:50,054
a limited time, and you can make a new one
whenever you need.

46
00:02:50,824 --> 00:02:51,726
Chidi: What is a share code?

47
00:02:52,446 --> 00:02:56,035
Kiran: Your digital handshake. You make it
on GOV.UK.

48
00:02:56,405 --> 00:03:01,575
Do it in your first days. Check your name,
your date of birth, and your passport

49
00:03:01,595 --> 00:03:06,441
details are exactly right. A tiny mistake
here can stop you renting a room,

50
00:03:06,461 --> 00:03:07,609
or starting a job.

51
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:12,837
And one thing that should make you feel
safer. The real share-code service

52
00:03:12,857 --> 00:03:16,267
is free, and it only lives on the official
GOV.UK website.

53
00:03:16,937 --> 00:03:21,819
This system is still changing, so check
the page called View and prove your

54
00:03:21,839 --> 00:03:25,087
immigration status on GOV.UK for the
latest steps.

55
00:03:26,557 --> 00:03:31,553
Step two. A phone number. You need one for
jobs, for the bank, for the doctor,

56
00:03:31,573 --> 00:03:32,968
for almost everything.

57
00:03:33,638 --> 00:03:37,365
And here is where people get trapped. A
phone shop will happily sell you a

58
00:03:37,385 --> 00:03:41,111
twenty-four month contract. That sounds
normal. It is not what you want in

59
00:03:41,131 --> 00:03:41,972
your first month.

60
00:03:42,742 --> 00:03:44,028
Chidi: Twenty-four months? Sign me up!

61
00:03:44,498 --> 00:03:46,026
Kiran: Chidi. Pen down. Now.

62
00:03:46,596 --> 00:03:51,152
You have no UK credit history yet. So a
contract can be refused, or come with

63
00:03:51,172 --> 00:03:55,787
a deposit. And if your job or your plans
change in two months... you are still

64
00:03:55,807 --> 00:03:57,392
paying for twenty-two more.

65
00:03:58,162 --> 00:04:03,125
Prices on some contracts also go up every
year. In the small print. Where nobody

66
00:04:03,145 --> 00:04:03,499
reads.

67
00:04:04,269 --> 00:04:09,892
Instead, buy a pay-as-you-go SIM or a
thirty-day rolling SIM-only plan.

68
00:04:09,912 --> 00:04:15,186
like giffgaff, Lebara, Lyca, Voxi, and
Asda Mobile are popular for this, and

69
00:04:15,206 --> 00:04:20,551
many don't run credit checks. Terms
change, so check the current offer before

70
00:04:20,571 --> 00:04:21,108
you buy.

71
00:04:21,878 --> 00:04:26,038
Thirty days. No chains. Stop any time.
Save the contract for later, when you

72
00:04:26,058 --> 00:04:29,558
have a credit history and you know exactly
where you are living.

73
00:04:30,878 --> 00:04:34,811
Step three. Where you sleep. And this is
the one place where being in a hurry

74
00:04:34,831 --> 00:04:35,581
costs the most.

75
00:04:36,252 --> 00:04:40,079
Mr Rush: Just send me the money today.
I'll keep the room for you. Cash is

76
00:04:40,099 --> 00:04:41,535
fine. No need for paperwork.

77
00:04:42,104 --> 00:04:43,476
Chidi: Cash is fine, he says! Easy!

78
00:04:43,946 --> 00:04:45,973
Kiran: Red flag. Giant red flag.

79
00:04:46,543 --> 00:04:50,649
Never. Never pay for a room you have not
seen. Never pay cash without a receipt.

80
00:04:50,669 --> 00:04:53,331
And never live anywhere without a written
agreement.

81
00:04:54,201 --> 00:04:58,422
A landlord will usually do a right-to-rent
check. That is where your share

82
00:04:58,442 --> 00:05:01,976
code comes in. It is normal. It is legal.
It is not an insult.

83
00:05:02,746 --> 00:05:06,876
When you pay a deposit, your landlord must
put it in a government-approved

84
00:05:06,896 --> 00:05:11,193
deposit scheme within thirty days, and
tell you which one. If they don't, you

85
00:05:11,213 --> 00:05:13,100
have rights, and you can get help.

86
00:05:13,869 --> 00:05:18,263
And a good sign of a legal landlord? A
calm one. Anyone who rushes you... is

87
00:05:18,283 --> 00:05:19,715
usually hiding something.

88
00:05:21,285 --> 00:05:26,464
Step four. A bank account. You cannot be
paid properly, or rent properly, without

89
00:05:26,484 --> 00:05:26,721
one.

90
00:05:27,391 --> 00:05:31,930
You have two main routes. A high-street
bank in person, or an app bank on your

91
00:05:31,950 --> 00:05:36,430
phone. Both will want to see your passport
or eVisa share code, and many will

92
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:37,891
ask for proof of address.

93
00:05:38,661 --> 00:05:43,331
Proof of address is where newcomers get
stuck. A tenancy agreement works. So

94
00:05:43,351 --> 00:05:47,960
can a letter from your employer, or your
college. Ask the bank exactly what

95
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,811
they accept, before you queue.

96
00:05:50,581 --> 00:05:55,553
If you are refused a normal account, ask
about a basic bank account. It has

97
00:05:55,573 --> 00:06:00,679
no overdraft, and no credit check. It is
designed for exactly this situation.

98
00:06:01,449 --> 00:06:06,072
And please, do not pay anyone to "arrange"
a bank account for you. It is free.

99
00:06:06,092 --> 00:06:07,500
It is your right to ask.

100
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:13,604
Step five. Your National Insurance number.
It is how the UK records your tax

101
00:06:13,624 --> 00:06:16,720
and your pension, and your employer will
ask for it.

102
00:06:17,391 --> 00:06:21,541
Here is what surprises almost everyone.
You do not need it to start work. You

103
00:06:21,561 --> 00:06:25,602
need your right to work. Your employer can
check that with your share code.

104
00:06:25,622 --> 00:06:27,552
Meanwhile, you apply for the number.

105
00:06:28,321 --> 00:06:33,280
You can only apply once you are in the UK,
and you do it on the official GOV.UK

106
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:38,008
website. It can take up to four weeks
after you prove your identity. Before

107
00:06:38,028 --> 00:06:42,672
you apply, check your documents. Some
people already have a number printed

108
00:06:42,692 --> 00:06:45,445
on their BRP, or inside their eVisa
account.

109
00:06:46,215 --> 00:06:51,836
Slick Sid: For £200, I can get your NI
number tomorrow. Very fast. Very special.

110
00:06:52,456 --> 00:06:54,002
Chidi: Fast-track? Two hundred pounds?
Take it!

111
00:06:54,472 --> 00:06:56,772
Kiran: Scam. The number is free. Always
free.

112
00:06:57,142 --> 00:07:01,564
That is a scam. A National Insurance
number is free. Always. Nobody can sell

113
00:07:01,584 --> 00:07:02,558
you a faster one.

114
00:07:03,428 --> 00:07:08,531
When you get your first payslip, read it.
Check your hours, your tax, and your

115
00:07:08,551 --> 00:07:13,720
pay. For anyone aged twenty-one and over,
the legal minimum right now is £12.71

116
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:18,646
an hour. If you are paid less than that,
you can get free help. These rates

117
00:07:18,666 --> 00:07:22,455
change every April, so check the current
figure on GOV.UK.

118
00:07:23,225 --> 00:07:27,969
And remember. In the UK, an employer is
not allowed to charge you for giving

119
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:28,596
you a job.

120
00:07:30,165 --> 00:07:35,169
Step six. A doctor. In the UK, your family
doctor is called a GP, and you must

121
00:07:35,189 --> 00:07:37,616
register with one before you need one.

122
00:07:38,286 --> 00:07:43,152
Registering is free. Use the NHS website
to find a surgery near where you live.

123
00:07:43,172 --> 00:07:44,636
Then fill in their form.

124
00:07:45,406 --> 00:07:50,158
And here is the thing the system does not
tell you. By the NHS's own guidance,

125
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:55,113
you do not need ID, proof of address, or
proof of immigration status to register.

126
00:07:55,983 --> 00:07:58,143
Kiran: No ID needed. Know your rights.

127
00:07:58,714 --> 00:08:02,993
Some receptionists will still ask for
them. If that happens, stay calm and

128
00:08:03,013 --> 00:08:07,350
politely say you know you do not need
them. If a surgery is full, they have

129
00:08:07,370 --> 00:08:11,882
to explain why, in writing. Charities like
Healthwatch can help you push back.

130
00:08:12,652 --> 00:08:17,945
For something urgent, but not life-
threatening, call 111. For an emergency,

131
00:08:17,965 --> 00:08:23,329
call 999. And for small problems, a
pharmacist is free to ask, and often the

132
00:08:23,349 --> 00:08:24,250
fastest help.

133
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:30,119
Step seven. Your phone is about to become
your toolbox. Let me show you what

134
00:08:30,139 --> 00:08:31,747
to install, today, for free.

135
00:08:32,368 --> 00:08:36,547
Indeed, for jobs. Search near where you
live. And a rule worth tattooing on

136
00:08:36,567 --> 00:08:40,747
your arm: a real employer never asks you
to pay to apply. Not for training.

137
00:08:40,767 --> 00:08:45,058
Not for a uniform. Not for a "background
check". If they ask for money, close

138
00:08:45,078 --> 00:08:45,506
the app.

139
00:08:46,175 --> 00:08:47,294
Chidi: Indeed! I am hired already!

140
00:08:47,765 --> 00:08:49,802
Kiran: Apply first, Chidi. Pay never.

141
00:08:50,322 --> 00:08:54,400
Google Maps. Not just for walking. Tap the
little bus symbol. It shows you

142
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:57,833
routes, the next departures, and the
walking time to the stop.

143
00:08:58,602 --> 00:09:04,255
Your local bus company almost always has
its own app, with live times and tickets.

144
00:09:04,275 --> 00:09:09,652
In big cities, Citymapper is brilliant.
For trains, use the Trainline, or your

145
00:09:09,672 --> 00:09:12,904
train company's app. And in London, use
TfL Go.

146
00:09:13,674 --> 00:09:18,549
Add the NHS App for your health records
and prescriptions once you are registered.

147
00:09:18,569 --> 00:09:22,549
Add a banking app. And keep the GOV.UK
website saved as a bookmark.

148
00:09:23,319 --> 00:09:27,132
Oh, and Vinted and Facebook Marketplace?
For the furniture you do not need

149
00:09:27,152 --> 00:09:29,049
to buy new. Remember the golden rule.

150
00:09:30,370 --> 00:09:34,557
Step eight. Your voice. But please listen
carefully, because this one is not

151
00:09:34,577 --> 00:09:35,830
the same for everybody.

152
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:40,987
You can register to vote if you are a
British citizen, an Irish citizen, or

153
00:09:41,007 --> 00:09:45,494
a citizen of a qualifying Commonwealth
country with permission to be in the

154
00:09:45,514 --> 00:09:45,614
UK

155
00:09:46,383 --> 00:09:51,006
Good news for many of you. India,
Pakistan, Bangladesh, Sri Lanka, Nigeria

156
00:09:51,026 --> 00:09:55,712
and Ghana are all Commonwealth countries.
So if you are a citizen of one of

157
00:09:55,732 --> 00:09:59,978
those, and you have permission to be here,
you can usually register.

158
00:10:00,749 --> 00:10:05,730
Nepal is not in the Commonwealth, so
Nepali citizens cannot vote here unless

159
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:10,665
they become British. And rules can differ
for each person. Check on GOV.UK,

160
00:10:10,685 --> 00:10:14,613
in the page called Register to vote,
before you do anything.

161
00:10:15,383 --> 00:10:19,135
And do not tick a box if you are not
eligible. Registering when you should

162
00:10:19,155 --> 00:10:19,899
not is a crime.

163
00:10:20,669 --> 00:10:25,437
If you are eligible, register. It takes
about five minutes, and it has a quiet

164
00:10:25,457 --> 00:10:30,102
bonus: being on the electoral roll helps
lenders confirm your address, which

165
00:10:30,122 --> 00:10:33,048
makes it easier to build a credit history
later.

166
00:10:34,518 --> 00:10:38,831
Before we go on, we need to talk about
scams. Because new arrivals are their

167
00:10:38,851 --> 00:10:39,857
favourite targets.

168
00:10:40,727 --> 00:10:44,785
Officer Fake: This is the Home Office.
There is a problem with your visa. You

169
00:10:44,805 --> 00:10:47,168
must pay immediately, or you will be
removed.

170
00:10:47,738 --> 00:10:49,047
Chidi: The Home Office! I will pay now!

171
00:10:49,317 --> 00:10:51,286
Kiran: Hang up. Breathe. Call a friend.

172
00:10:51,856 --> 00:10:55,895
That is not the Home Office. The Home
Office says it will never ask you to

173
00:10:55,915 --> 00:10:58,418
pay by email, or into a personal bank
account.

174
00:10:59,287 --> 00:11:03,342
Here is the pattern. Scammers promise you
something you desperately want. A

175
00:11:03,362 --> 00:11:07,418
job. A visa. A room. A number. And they
ask you to pay first. They want you

176
00:11:07,438 --> 00:11:09,374
to rush. They want you to be scared.

177
00:11:10,145 --> 00:11:14,640
Every year, hardworking people lose their
savings to these promises. And many

178
00:11:14,660 --> 00:11:16,517
feel too ashamed to tell anyone.

179
00:11:17,536 --> 00:11:22,303
One more, especially for people coming for
care work and other sponsored jobs.

180
00:11:22,323 --> 00:11:26,844
Before you pay anything, or even trust an
offer, check the employer on the

181
00:11:26,864 --> 00:11:31,385
official Register of Licensed Sponsors on
GOV.UK. If the company is not on

182
00:11:31,405 --> 00:11:32,981
it, it cannot sponsor you.

183
00:11:33,751 --> 00:11:38,084
You are not stupid, and you are not alone.
If something feels wrong, stop.

184
00:11:38,104 --> 00:11:42,495
Take a breath. Ask a friend. And if you
have been tricked, report it to the

185
00:11:42,515 --> 00:11:46,965
police fraud service, or ask Citizens
Advice or Migrant Help. They are free.

186
00:11:47,735 --> 00:11:52,115
The golden rule for scams? Anything real
is free, or can wait for a day.

187
00:11:53,435 --> 00:11:56,945
Once those basics are done, there are a
few more things worth knowing.

188
00:11:57,615 --> 00:12:01,574
Your local council will want you
registered for council tax, and there may

189
00:12:01,594 --> 00:12:05,445
be discounts, for example if you live
alone. Don't ignore their letters.

190
00:12:06,215 --> 00:12:10,944
If you drive, a licence from outside
Europe can usually be used for twelve

191
00:12:10,964 --> 00:12:16,014
months. After that you need a UK licence.
For most of our countries, that means

192
00:12:16,034 --> 00:12:20,955
passing the UK driving test, so book your
theory test early. Check GOV.UK for

193
00:12:20,975 --> 00:12:23,715
your own country, because the rules
differ.

194
00:12:24,484 --> 00:12:29,053
If you have children, you apply for a
school place through your local council.

195
00:12:29,073 --> 00:12:33,878
And you only need a TV licence if you
watch live television, or the BBC's catch-

196
00:12:33,898 --> 00:12:34,349
service.

197
00:12:35,119 --> 00:12:39,341
And find a free English class near you.
Even a little improves your confidence,

198
00:12:39,361 --> 00:12:41,220
your job options, and your friends.

199
00:12:42,541 --> 00:12:44,221
So let us put it all together.

200
00:12:44,891 --> 00:12:50,658
Days one to three: your eVisa and share
code, a cheap SIM, and a safe place

201
00:12:50,678 --> 00:12:51,352
to sleep.

202
00:12:52,121 --> 00:12:55,538
Week one: a bank account, and your GP.

203
00:12:56,308 --> 00:13:01,358
Weeks two to four: your National Insurance
number, your job applications, and

204
00:13:01,378 --> 00:13:03,399
your vote, if you are eligible.

205
00:13:04,170 --> 00:13:08,746
And in months two and three, when you have
a job and an address, that is the

206
00:13:08,766 --> 00:13:12,435
time to think about credit, a contract, or
a bigger purchase.

207
00:13:13,204 --> 00:13:17,886
Notice what is not on the list. A new
phone. A new laptop. A new sofa. They

208
00:13:17,906 --> 00:13:18,450
can wait.

209
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,665
Chidi: Not even a small phone?

210
00:13:21,535 --> 00:13:23,807
Kiran: Day thirty-one, Chidi. Day thirty-
one.

211
00:13:24,327 --> 00:13:29,825
And one last time, because it matters.
This is general information, correct

212
00:13:29,845 --> 00:13:35,564
as of November 2026. It is not legal
advice. Rules, fees and processes change,

213
00:13:35,584 --> 00:13:41,156
so always check GOV.UK before you act. If
your situation is complicated, ask

214
00:13:41,176 --> 00:13:44,982
Citizens Advice, or a regulated
immigration adviser.

215
00:13:45,752 --> 00:13:49,693
Starting in a new country is one of the
bravest things a person can do. It

216
